-- title:
--   Class-set dictionary for the Bruhat–Tits quotient at r
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $H := \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ is the quaternion algebra attached to two rationals $a_1, b_1$, and $\mathrm{Cl}(U)$ denotes `ClassSet U`, the double coset space of the finite idele units $(H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}})^{\times}$ by the diagonal image of $H^{\times}$ on the left and a subgroup $U$ on the right.
--
--   *Numerical data.* A non-zero squarefree natural number $N$; primes $q, q'$ with $q' \neq q$, neither dividing $N$, both at least $5$; primes $r, \bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, neither dividing $N$, both at least $5$. The hypothesis `hdef₁` asserts `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a₁ b₁ rbar`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every non-zero element of $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $\bar r \in v$.
--
--   *Orders and the level-raising idele at $r$.* $\Lambda_1, R_1$ are $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $H$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order (an order which is maximal among orders for inclusion), $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders whose relative index in the first is $N$), and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$. The finite idele unit $n_1$ lies in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r`, i.e. $n_1$ and $r \cdot n_1^{-1}$ lie in the finite adelic box of $R_1$ while $n_1^{-1}$ and $r^{-1} n_1$ do not. Write $S_1 :=$ `meetOrder R₁ n₁` $= R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ (the conjugate being formed by [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31)). The hypotheses on $S_1$ are: `hS₁`, that $S_1$ is an Eichler order of level $N r$; `hnorm₁`, that conjugation by $n_1$ fixes $S_1$; and `hsq₁`, that the shift $x \mapsto \mathrm{mk}(x_{\mathrm{out}} \cdot n_1)$ on $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(S_1))$ is an involution, where $\mathrm{Stab}(\cdot)$ denotes [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26). The class sets $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(S_1))$ and $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(R_1))$ are assumed finite.
--
--   *The place above $r$ and the splitting.* $A_2$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hA₂ : A₂.LiesOverPrime r`, i.e. $r$ is a non-unit of $A_2$; $v_2$ is a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $r \in v_2$. Put $K_0 :=$ [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13), the topological closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $A_2$'s valuation. The map $\iota_2 : H \to M_2(K_0)$ is an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism, and $\rho_2 : H^{\times} \to \mathrm{PGL}(2, K_0)$ is the homomorphism which, by `hρ₂`, sends $x$ to the projective class of the matrix unit obtained by applying $\iota_2$ to $x$.
--
--   *Level-raising elements away from $q, q'$.* For $\ell$ ranging over `HeckeTower.AwayPrime q q'`, the primes different from $q$ and $q'$, there are given $s_2(\ell) \in H^{\times}$ and finite idele units $\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell)$; the hypothesis `hs₂` requires, for each such $\ell$: the $u$-component of $\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell)$ equals $s_2(\ell) \otimes 1$ at every prime $u$ with $r \notin u$, and equals $1$ at every $u$ with $r \in u$; the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ S₁ ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ (that is, in `primeHeckeSet S₁ ℓ` and such that conjugation by it moves $S_1$ and such that $S_1$ is not contained in the conjugate of $\Lambda_1$), and in `primeHeckeSet S₁ ℓ` otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_2(\ell)) = \ell$.
--
--   *Atkin–Lehner elements.* Two families $w_2, \bar w_2$ indexed by `HeckeTower.Obj q q'` $=$ `Option (HeckeTower.AwayPrime q q')` with values in $H^{\times}$. The hypothesis `hw₂` says that $w_2(\mathrm{none})$ lies in `awayUnits R₁ v₂` — the subgroup of $x \in H^{\times}$ whose image in $(H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_u)^{\times}$ lies in the subgroup generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R₁ u`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) for every prime $u \neq v_2$ — and has reduced norm $r$, and that for each $\ell$ the element $w_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ lies in `awayUnits (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) v₂` and has reduced norm $r$. The hypothesis `hwbar₂` says that $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$ has reduced norm $\bar r$, that its image in $(H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_u)^{\times}$ lies in `localBoxUnits R₁ u` for every $u \neq v_2$ with $\bar r \notin u$, and that for every $u \neq v_2$ conjugation by it preserves both `localBox R₁ u` and `localBox Λ₁ u` (as two-sided membership equivalences); the same three conditions are required of each $\bar w_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$, with $R_1$ replaced by `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)` in the first two and $\Lambda_1$ unchanged in the last.
--
--   *The coefficient ring.* $R_0$ is a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, is an algebra over $K_0$'s ring of elements with $K_0$ as fraction field, and, by `hR₀`, has image in $K_0$ exactly the elements of valuation at most $1$ after passing to the completion of $A_2$'s valuation.
--
--   *Tower data at the auxiliary primes.* For each $\ell$ as above: `hR'` says `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)` is an Eichler order of level $N \ell$; $n'(\ell)$ is a finite idele unit in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) r`; `hS'` says `meetOrder (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) (n' ℓ)` is an Eichler order of level $N \ell r$; `hnorm'` says conjugation by $n'(\ell)$ fixes that doubly met order; `hsq'` says the shift by $n'(\ell)$ is an involution on its class set; `hnn'` says $n_1^{-1} n'(\ell) \in \mathrm{Stab}(R_1)$; and `hsn'` says $\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell)$ and $n'(\ell)$ commute. The class sets of $\mathrm{Stab}(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell))$ and of $\mathrm{Stab}(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell))\,n'(\ell))$ are assumed finite.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Let $\Delta :=$ `(CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂).map ρ₂`, the image of the $v_2$-away unit group in $\mathrm{PGL}(2, K_0)$, acting on the homothety classes [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex R₀ K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) of full $R_0$-lattices in $K_0^2$ and on the Bruhat–Tits graph $\mathcal{T} :=$ `BruhatTits.tree R₀ K₀` built from the adjacency relation of lattices. Then there exist bijections
--   $$\varepsilon_V : \Delta \backslash \mathrm{Vert}(\mathcal{T}) \;\simeq\; \mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(R_1)), \qquad \varepsilon_E : \Delta \backslash \mathrm{Dart}(\mathcal{T}) \;\simeq\; \mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(S_1))$$
--   (the orbit quotients of the vertex set and of the dart set) such that the following six assertions hold.
--
--   (1) For every dart orbit $e$, $\varepsilon_V$ of the origin map of `Mumford.quotientDegeneracyData Δ 𝒯` applied to $e$ — the orbit of the first vertex of a dart — equals the $a$-map of `classSetDegeneracyData R₁ n₁` applied to $\varepsilon_E(e)$, namely `classSetForget`, the passage of a representative idele to its class modulo $\mathrm{Stab}(R_1)$.
--
--   (2) For every dart orbit $e$, $\varepsilon_V$ of the terminus map of `Mumford.quotientDegeneracyData Δ 𝒯` applied to $e$ — the orbit of the second vertex of a dart — equals the $b$-map of `classSetDegeneracyData R₁ n₁` applied to $\varepsilon_E(e)$, namely $x \mapsto \mathrm{mk}(x_{\mathrm{out}} \cdot n_1)$ in $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(R_1))$.
--
--   (3) For every dart $d$ of $\mathcal{T}$, the cardinality of the stabiliser of $d$ in $\Delta$ equals the weight $w$ of `classSetDegeneracyData R₁ n₁` at $\varepsilon_E$ of the orbit of $d$, that is `classWeight` of $S_1$ at that class: the positive integer `unitWeight` of the conjugate of $S_1$ by a representative idele of the class.
--
--   (4) For every dart $d$, $\varepsilon_E$ of the orbit of the reversed dart $d^{\mathrm{symm}}$ equals `classSetShift (Stab S₁) n₁` applied to $\varepsilon_E$ of the orbit of $d$, i.e. the shift $x \mapsto \mathrm{mk}(x_{\mathrm{out}} \cdot n_1)$ within $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(S_1))$.
--
--   (5) There exists a finite idele unit $\varpi'$ with: all components of $\varpi'$ at primes $w$ with $\bar r \notin w$ equal to $1$; $\varpi' \in$ `primeHeckeSet S₁ rbar`; conjugation by $\varpi'$ fixing $S_1$; the shift by $\varpi'$ an involution on $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathrm{Stab}(S_1))$; and, for every dart $d$, $\varepsilon_E$ of the orbit of $\rho_2(\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})) \cdot d$ equal to the shift by $\varpi'$ of $\varepsilon_E$ of the orbit of $d$.
--
--   (6) For every prime $\ell$ different from $q$ and $q'$, writing $\Delta_\ell :=$ `(awayUnits (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) v₂).map ρ₂`, there exists a bijection
--   $$\varepsilon_E'' : \Delta_\ell \backslash \mathrm{Dart}(\mathcal{T}) \;\simeq\; \mathrm{Cl}\bigl(\mathrm{Stab}(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,\mathrm{sf}_2(\ell))\,n'(\ell))\bigr)$$
--   such that: (i) for every dart $d$, the cardinality of the stabiliser of $d$ in $\Delta_\ell$ equals the weight $w$ of `classSetDegeneracyData (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) (n' ℓ)` at $\varepsilon_E''$ of the $\Delta_\ell$-orbit of $d$; (ii) for every dart $d$, $\varepsilon_E$ of the $\Delta$-orbit of $d$ is the image under `classSetForget` of $\varepsilon_E''$ of the $\Delta_\ell$-orbit of $d$; and (iii) for every dart $d$, $\varepsilon_E$ of the $\Delta$-orbit of $\rho_2(s_2(\ell))^{-1} \cdot d$ is the class of $x_{\mathrm{out}} \cdot \mathrm{sf}_2(\ell)$, where $x = \varepsilon_E''$ of the $\Delta_\ell$-orbit of $d$.
--
--   This is the class-set dictionary for the Čerednik–Drinfeld picture at a place above $r$: it identifies the quotient of the Bruhat–Tits tree by the image of the $v_2$-away unit group of an Eichler order with the degeneracy data built from the class sets of that order and of its level-$Nr$ meet order, together with the compatibilities needed to read off dart reversal, the Atkin–Lehner translate at $\bar r$, and the level-$\ell$ forget and shift maps. It is the input to the statements that compare realisations of the quotient graph along the Hecke tower and that produce quotient presentations of class-set Hecke data.
